; 43c's secure referral, made answerable. The parent's delegation for `secure`
; is in the zone response_size.rs measures; what that zone does not have is a
; child a validator can actually reach, so this is one. rdnsd signs it and
; setup() puts its real DS into the parent, which is what makes the referral a
; chain rather than an assertion.
$ORIGIN secure.example.net.
$TTL 3600
@    IN SOA ns.secure.example.net. hostmaster.example.net. ( 2026091101 3600 600 604800 300 )
@    IN NS  ns.secure.example.net.
ns   IN A   10.53.0.11
www  IN A   192.0.2.203
